A column renamed in schema.sql and nothing more: to SQLite's listings, one
column gone and another new. Refused, since the old one's values would
go; the table has one new column, so the error writes the rename step with
both names, ready to paste into ledger.sql.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '') STRICT;

== error
column `dish.title` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its values would go. Renamed? Add the step to ledger.sql: `ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;` Gone on purpose? `ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN title;`
